"You apparently have called the function '{fn_name}' with\n"
"fewer positional arguments than it requires ({nb_required} missing).\n"
msgstr ""
"Aftidan, siz '{fn_name}' funksiyasini u talab qilganidan\n"
"kamroq pozitsion argument bilan çaqirgansiz ({nb_required} tasi yetişmayapti).\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:546 runtime_errors\type_error.py:934 warning_parsers\syntax_warning.py:21
#: warning_parsers\syntax_warning.py:69
msgid ""
"\n"
"Note: `NoneType` means that the object has a value of `None`.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Izoh: `NoneType` obyektning qiymati `None` ekanini bildiradi.\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:553 warning_parsers\syntax_warning.py:27
msgid ""
"Python indicates that you have an object of type `{obj_type}`,\n"
"followed by something surrounded by parentheses, `(...)`,\n"
"which Python took as an indication of a function call.\n"
"Either the object of type `{obj_type}` was meant to be a function,\n"
"or you forgot a comma before `(...)`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Python sizda `{obj_type}` turidagi obyekt va undan keyin\n"
"qavslar içiga olingan `(...)` narsa borligini körsatyapti,\n"
"Python buni funksiya çaqiruvi belgisi deb tuşundi.\n"
"Yo `{obj_type}` turidagi obyekt funksiya bölişi kerak edi,\n"
"yoki `(...)` dan oldin vergul qöyişni unutgansiz.\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:580
msgid ""
"The parenthesis `()` following `{obj_name}` are interpreted\n"
"by Python as a function call for `{obj_name}`.\n"
"However, `{obj_name}` is not a function but an object of type `{obj_type}`.\n"
msgstr ""
"`{obj_name}` dan keyingi `()` qavslarini Python\n"
"`{obj_name}` uçun funksiya çaqiruvi deb tuşunadi.\n"
"Biroq `{obj_name}` funksiya emas, `{obj_type}` turidagi obyekt.\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:587
msgid ""
"Because of the surrounding parenthesis, `{fn_call}` \n"
"is interpreted by Python as indicating a function call for \n"
"`{obj_name}`, which is an object of type `{obj_type}`\n"
"which cannot be called.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"Atrofidagi qavslar tufayli Python `{fn_call}` ni\n"
"`{obj_name}` uçun funksiya çaqiruvi deb tuşunadi,\n"
"u esa `{obj_type}` turidagi obyekt bölib,\n"
"uni çaqirib bölmaydi.\n"
"\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:600
msgid ""
"However, `{fn_call}` is a `tuple`.\n"
"Either the object `{obj_name}` was meant to be a function\n"
"or you have a missing comma between the object `{obj_name}`\n"
"and the tuple `{fn_call}` and meant to write\n"
"`{obj_name}, {fn_call}`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Biroq `{fn_call}` — `tuple` (kortej).\n"
"Yo `{obj_name}` obyekti funksiya bölişi kerak edi,\n"
"yoki `{obj_name}` obyekti va `{fn_call}` korteji orasida vergul\n"
"tuşib qolgan va siz `{obj_name}, {fn_call}` deb\n"
"yozmoqçi bölgansiz.\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:607
msgid "Did you forget a comma between `{obj_name}` and `{fn_call}`?\n"
msgstr "`{obj_name}` va `{fn_call}` orasida vergul qöyişni unutdingizmi?\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:613
msgid ""
"However, `{obj_name}` is a sequence.\n"
"Perhaps you meant to use `[]` instead of `()` and write\n"
"`{obj_name}[{slice}]`\n"
msgstr ""
"Biroq `{obj_name}` — ketma-ketlik.\n"
"Ehtimol, siz `()` örniga `[]` dan foydalanib,\n"
"`{obj_name}[{slice}]` deb yozmoqçi bölgandirsiz.\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:618
msgid "Did you mean `{obj_name}[{slice}]`?\n"
msgstr "`{obj_name}[{slice}]` ni nazarda tutdingizmi?\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:629
msgid ""
"However, both `{obj_name}` and `{fn_call}` are numbers.\n"
"Perhaps you forgot a multiplication operator, `*`,\n"
"and meant to write `{obj_name} * {fn_call}`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Biroq `{obj_name}` ham, `{fn_call}` ham sonlar.\n"
"Ehtimol, siz köpaytiriş operatori `*` ni unutib,\n"
"`{obj_name} * {fn_call}` deb yozmoqçi bölgandirsiz.\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:634
msgid "Did you mean `{obj_name} * {fn_call}`?\n"
msgstr "`{obj_name} * {fn_call}` ni nazarda tutdingizmi?\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:646
msgid "Did you forget to convert `{name}` into an integer?\n"
msgstr "`{name}` ni butun songa aylantirişni unutdingizmi?\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:647
msgid "Perhaps you forgot to convert `{name}` into an integer.\n"
msgstr "Ehtimol, `{name}` ni butun songa aylantirişni unutgandirsiz.\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:659
msgid ""
"You can only multiply sequences, such as list, tuples,\n"
" strings, etc., by integers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Röyxat, kortej, satr va hokazo kabi ketma-ketliklarni\n"
" faqat butun sonlarga köpaytiriş mumkin.\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:681
msgid "Did you forget to convert `{name1}` and `{name2}` into integers?\n"
msgstr "`{name1}` va `{name2}` ni butun sonlarga aylantirişni unutdingizmi?\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:684
msgid "Perhaps you forgot to convert `{name1}` and `{name2}` into integers.\n"
msgstr "Ehtimol, `{name1}` va `{name2}` ni butun sonlarga aylantirişni unutgandirsiz.\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:720
msgid "You wrote an object whose value is `None` where an integer was expected.\n"
msgstr "Siz butun son kutilgan joyga qiymati `None` bölgan obyektni yozdingiz.\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:730
msgid "You wrote an object of type `{obj}` where an integer was expected.\n"
msgstr "Siz butun son kutilgan joyga `{obj}` turidagi obyektni yozdingiz.\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:740
msgid "Did you forget to convert `{names}` into integers?\n"
msgstr "`{names}` ni butun sonlarga aylantirişni unutdingizmi?\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:743
msgid "Perhaps you forgot to convert `{names}` into integers."
msgstr "Ehtimol, `{names}` ni butun sonlarga aylantirişni unutgandirsiz."

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:766
msgid ""
"In the expression `{line}`\n"
"what is included between the square brackets, `[...]`,\n"
"must be either an integer or a slice\n"
"(`start:stop` or `start:stop:step`) \n"
"and you have used {obj_type} instead.\n"
msgstr ""
"`{line}` ifodasida\n"
"kvadrat qavslar `[...]` orasidagi narsa butun son yoki kesim\n"
"(`start:stop` yoki `start:stop:step`) bölişi kerak,\n"
"siz esa buning örniga {obj_type} işlatgansiz.\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:777
msgid ""
"Note: sometimes this exception is raised because what Python\n"
"interprets as indices was meant to be a separate list, and a comma\n"
"should have been written before the opening `[` of that list.\n"
msgstr ""
"Izoh: baʼzan bu istisno Python indeks deb tuşungan narsa aslida\n"
"alohida röyxat bölişi kerak bölgani uçun yuzaga keladi va şu röyxatning\n"
"oçuvçi `[` qavsidan oldin vergul yozilişi kerak edi.\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:782 syntax_errors\statement_analyzer.py:1187 syntax_errors\statement_analyzer.py:1559
msgid "Did you forget a comma?\n"
msgstr "Vergulni unutdingizmi?\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:817
msgid ""
"Perhaps you have forgotten a comma between two identical lists\n"
"`{container}`. The second list had been interpreted as\n"
"the indexation of the first one by the index `{new_index}`\n"
msgstr ""
"Ehtimol, ikki bir xil `{container}` röyxati orasida vergulni unutgandirsiz.\n"
"Ikkinçi röyxat birinçisini `{new_index}` indeksi böyiça\n"
"indekslaş deb tuşunilgan.\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:823
msgid ""
"Perhaps you have forgotten a comma between the object `{container}`\n"
"and the list `{index}`.  The list `{index}` had been interpreted as\n"
"the indexation of object `{container}` by the index `{new_index}`\n"
msgstr ""
"Ehtimol, `{container}` obyekti va `{index}` röyxati orasida vergulni unutgandirsiz.\n"
"`{index}` röyxati `{container}` obyektini `{new_index}` indeksi böyiça\n"
"indekslaş deb tuşunilgan.\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:828
msgid "Did you forget a comma before `{index}`?\n"
msgstr "`{index}` dan oldin vergulni unutdingizmi?\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:887
msgid ""
"When using a slice to extract a range of elements\n"
"from a sequence, that is something like\n"
"`[start:stop]` or `[start:stop:step]`\n"
"each of `start`, `stop`, `step` must be either an integer, `None`,\n"
"or possibly some other object having an `__index__` method.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ketma-ketlikdan elementlar oraliğini ajratib oliş uçun kesimdan,\n"
"yaʼni `[start:stop]` yoki `[start:stop:step]` ga öxşaş narsadan\n"
"foydalanganda `start`, `stop`, `step` ning har biri butun son, `None`\n"
"yoki `__index__` metodiga ega boşqa obyekt bölişi kerak.\n"

#: runtime_errors\type_error.py:904
msgid ""
"Only hashable objects can be used\n"
"as elements of `set` or keys of `dict`.\n"
"Hashable objects are objects that do not change value\n"
"once they have been created."
msgstr ""
